  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Intransitive godan verb. X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{休|やす}まる, typically with ⟦{気|き}→気：02199_ki⟧, ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧, or ⟦{体|からだ}→体：00784_karada⟧ as the subject. The transitive pair is ⟦{休|やす}める→休める：02437_yasumeru⟧ (to rest something).\n\nDescribes tension and fatigue being relieved. Very often in the phrase ⟦{気|き}→気：02199_ki⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{休|やす}まる.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{気|き}→気：02199_ki⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{休|やす}まる: to feel at ease\n- ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{休|やす}まる: one's mind is at rest\n- ⟦{体|からだ}→体：00784_karada⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{休|やす}まる: one's body gets a rest\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{休|やす}む→休む：00606_yasumu⟧: to rest — the basic verb; an action one does, whereas {休|やす}まる is a state one comes into\n- ⟦くつろぐ→くつろぐ：02576_kutsurogu⟧: to relax — to make oneself comfortable and unwind",
